{"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Swift\/Never\/defaultPosition(_:)"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Swift","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Swift\/Never"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM","kind":"attribute","text":"MainActor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"defaultPosition"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"_"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"position"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI9UnitPointV","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint","text":"UnitPoint"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI5SceneP","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Scene","text":"Scene"},{"kind":"text","text":"\n"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"parameters":[{"name":"position","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" that specifies where to place a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"newly opened window relative to the screen bounds."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"parameters"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A scene that uses a default position for new windows.","type":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The first time your app opens a window from a particular scene","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"declaration, the system places the window at the center of the screen by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"default. For scene types that support multiple simultaneous windows, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"system offsets each additional window by a small amount to avoid","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"completely obscuring existing windows.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You can override the default placement of the first window by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"applying a scene modifier that indicates where to place the window","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"relative to the screen bounds. For example, you can request that the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"system place a new window in the bottom trailing corner of the screen:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["@main","struct MyApp: App {","    var body: some Scene {","        WindowGroup {","            ContentView()","        }","        .defaultPosition(.bottomTrailing)","    }","}"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The system aligns the point in the window that corresponds to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"specified ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint","type":"reference"},{"text":" with the point in the screen that corresponds","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the same unit point.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You typically use one of the predefined unit points — like","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint\/bottomTrailing","type":"reference"},{"text":" in the above example — but","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"you can also use a custom unit point. For example, the following","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"modifier aligns the point that’s one quarter of the way from the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"leading edge of the window with the point that’s one quarter of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the way from the leading edge of the screen, while centering the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"window in the y-dimension:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["WindowGroup {","    ContentView()","}",".defaultPosition(UnitPoint(x: 0.25, y: 0.5))"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The modifier affects any scene type that creates windows in Windows,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"namely:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup","isActive":true}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Window","isActive":true}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DocumentGroup"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Settings","isActive":true}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The value that you provide acts only as an initial default. During state","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"restoration, the system restores the window to the position that it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"last occupied.","type":"text"}]}]}],"metadata"